  "observe": {
    "chatId": "2026-10-01@23h41m44s699ms",
    "groupId": "1790908516372",
    "group": "Adolion - The Eastern Road",
    "storyId": "adolion-east",
    "activeCheckpointId": "east-the-rounds",
    "boundary": 10,
    "folded": null,
    "payloadEpoch": "1790908915383-dymm5a",
    "context": [
      {
        "id": 6,
        "name": "Honami",
        "isUser": false,
        "text": "\"It certainly is,\" she says with a graceful nod, gesturing toward the imposing dark timber halls and stone courtyards. \"The tournament register is managed by a senior administrator—a rather dull man, but efficient enough. You'll find him in the main hall.\"\n*She walks closer to Max, one white tail casually brushing against his arm as she speaks.*\n\"As for favourites...\" Her red eyes glint with something sharp beneath her sweet expression. \"Many would say Megumi-san is the one to beat. But I believe that is a matter of opinion rather than fact.\" She smiles, her gaze never leaving Max. \"Though I must confess, I find the odds far more interesting when they're... uncertain. Perhaps a new group entry could provide just the upset the Academy needs.\""
      },
      {
        "id": 7,
        "name": "Max Nightriver",
        "isUser": true,
        "text": "*I walk into the main hall to the administrator's desk.* We're here for the tournament. Put our names on the register under Honami Nemaden's, and tell me who that grey-haired steward by the door is."
      },
      {
        "id": 8,
        "name": "Adolion Narrator",
        "isUser": false,
        "text": "The main hall is cavernous and silent, the air heavy with incense and the scent of polished cedar. A senior administrator sits behind a long desk of dark lacquer, his face as lined and expressionless as a riverbed. He does not look up as Max approaches, merely dips a brush into ink and waits.\nThe administrator's hand pauses. \"Honami Nemaden-sama, yes,\" he says in a dry rasp, finally meeting Max's eyes. \"Your group's entry papers were... expedited.\" His brush moves with practiced efficiency across the register. \"As for that gentleman,\" he glances toward the door without turning his head, \"that is Lord Karos. He is here for his own reasons.\""
      },
      {
        "id": 9,
        "name": "Megumi",
        "isUser": false,
        "text": "\"Welcome to Jiansho Academy! I'm Megumi Xianxu, Head of the Student Council.\" The smile is flawless; behind her back, her hands are wringing the spine of a register book. \"And you must be Honami's... guests. How brave of you. Shall I read you the rules before you sign, or after?\""
      },
      {
        "id": 10,
        "name": "Honami",
        "isUser": false,
        "text": "\"Lord Karos?\" Honami steps closer to Max, her voice hushed and curious. Her white hair shifts across her face as she glances toward the silver-haired man by the door. \"How peculiar. I wasn't aware he had any interest in the tournament.\"\n*Her tails flick with subtle intrigue, though her gaze remains fixed on Max, as if checking his reaction. One tail curls forward, almost touching his arm in a possessive gesture.*\n\"You have a keen eye, Darling,\" she murmurs, her smile prim and sweet. \"Most would have been too preoccupied with the register to notice a steward standing guard.\""
      },
      {
        "id": 11,
        "name": "Adolion Narrator",
        "isUser": false,
        "text": "A bronze gong rolls across the sand. \"Group entry, Honami Nemaden and the guests of Darran, against the Mountain Silence of the Guao!\" A steward lights the first incense stick, and the noise of the stands drops to a hum."
      },
      {
        "id": 12,
        "name": "Max Nightriver",
        "isUser": true,
        "text": "*We step onto the sand for our first bout of the Jiansho Tournament.* Belle, you take the big one. Dalan, watch the flank. Let's show the Guao what the Guild sends."
      },
      {
        "id": 13,
        "name": "Belle",
        "isUser": false,
        "text": "\"Got it.\" Belle doesn't wait for the gong to fade before she's already moving, Cleaver's head scraping the sand. \"And you stay back and watch, pretty boy. Wouldn't want that fancy Nightriver blood getting splattered on the place.\"\n*She doesn't look back, just shifts her weight and grins as her opponent steps forward—a hulking monk who barely reaches her shoulder but moves with the solid confidence of a mountain. Belle's brown eyes gleam with something hungry.*\n\"Try not to blink too much,\" she adds over her shoulder, \"or you'll miss the best part.\""
      }
    ]
  }
}
